  "system": {
    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Galaxy_at_War\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy at War\">Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy at War</a></i> </p><p>Found on primitive planets where Slugthrowers are still used, the Scattergun is a large-barreled, low-velocity Slugthrower that launches a blast of pellets spreading out over a distance. Scattergun and their ammunition are cheap to manufacture and are primarily used for hunting. </p><p>However, mercenaries, marines, and other soldiers sometimes carry a Scattergun as a backup weapon for facing enemies in close quarters or for clearing rooms in house-to-house fighting. Scatterguns deal 3d8 points of damage at Point-Blank <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Range\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Range\">Range</a>, 2d8 points of damage at Short <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Range\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Range\">Range</a>, and no damage at Medium or Long <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Range\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Range\">Range</a>. </p><p>Scatterguns do not need <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Power_Packs\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Power Packs\">Power Packs</a>. Instead, they fire individual shells. Scatterguns hold 10 shells that each cost 2 credits and weigh 0.1 kg. </p><p><b>Special:</b> Scatter Guns cannot fire at targets at Medium or Long <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Range\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Range\">Range</a>.&nbsp; </p>",
